{"uid":"modules/loop_manager.py","name":"loop_manager.py","qualname":"modules/loop_manager.py","kind":"module","file":"modules/loop_manager.py","line":1,"end_line":811,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Parallel autonomous loop orchestration for the LazyOwn C2 dashboard.","description":"Contract: this module owns every autonomous loop started from the web\ndashboard. Each loop is an isolated ``lazyown.py`` subprocess (argv form,\n``shell=False``, own process session) with a dedicated workspace under\n``sessions/loops/<loop_id>/`` holding its YAML profile, live output log\nand metadata. A single JSON registry (``sessions/loops/registry.json``)\nis the durable source of truth so loops survive dashboard restarts.\n\nInvariants:\n\n1. Every user-supplied field is strictly validated before it can reach\n   a subprocess: the target must parse as an IP address, the goal must\n   match a fixed safe charset, and numeric knobs are clamped to the\n   ranges supported by :mod:`modules.lazy_runner`.\n2. Subprocesses are never started through a shell. ``argv`` lists only,\n   ``shell=False``, ``stdin=DEVNULL`` and ``start_new_session=True`` so\n   a loop can be stopped as a whole process group.\n3. Log reads are path-safe: the loop id must match a strict hex pattern\n   and the resolved log path must stay inside the loops directory.\n4. The number of concurrently running loops is capped so the dashboard\n   can never exhaust host processes.\n5. Stop uses SIGTERM on the process group, waits a grace period, then\n   escalates to SIGKILL. A stored process start-time counter prevents\n   acting on a recycled PID.\n\nConfig keys owned: none (all knobs are module constants).","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["modules/loop_manager.py::KIND_AUTO_LOOP","modules/loop_manager.py::KIND_LAZY_NMAP","modules/loop_manager.py::LOOP_KINDS","modules/loop_manager.py::DEFAULT_ROUNDS","modules/loop_manager.py::DEFAULT_WORKERS","modules/loop_manager.py::MAX_ROUNDS","modules/loop_manager.py::MAX_WORKERS","modules/loop_manager.py::MAX_CONCURRENT_LOOPS","modules/loop_manager.py::DEFAULT_GOAL","modules/loop_manager.py::LoopValidationError","modules/loop_manager.py::LoopNotFoundError","modules/loop_manager.py::validate_target","modules/loop_manager.py::sanitize_goal","modules/loop_manager.py::clamp_int","modules/loop_manager.py::clamp_float","modules/loop_manager.py::LoopSpec","modules/loop_manager.py::LoopManager"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
